    {
      "name": "DpvResource",
      "definition_uri": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/dpv/DpvResource",
      "description": "A thing a use case describes with DPV, such as a process, holding any DPV property, because DPV states none as limited to a class.",
      "title": "Resource",
      "comments": [
        "DPV's domainIncludes and rangeIncludes say what a property usually joins, not what it must, so a validator cannot refuse a value on them. tests/dpv_rules.py reports a value that names nothing, and tests/test_examples.py lists where DPV's own examples leave those classes."
      ],
      "from_schema": "https://w3id.org/lmodel/dpv/dpv_terms",
      "exact_mappings": [
        "rdfs:Resource"
      ],
